## Core Concepts

### Blueprint‑First Design
High‑level electronic intent → structured blueprint → simulation‑ready model.

### Lightweight Simulation Kernel
The kernel steps through circuits, components, and signal states.

### Structural Authorship Encoding
Identity is embedded in:
- Manifests  
- Kernel metadata  
- Simulation configs  
- Exported reports  

### Minimal, Expandable Architecture
The system is intentionally small and modular so it can grow inside the Codex without conflicts.

